---
# Two relaxations, both for the same reason: this directory is where vector
# intrinsics are written, and the checks below describe the boundary the rest
# of the tree keeps rather than anything wrong here.
#
# pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic - Highway's loads take a raw pointer and an
# index, and stepping one by a register width is what a kernel is. The public
# API in ladder.hpp takes std::span, so the bounds are checked once at the
# boundary and the arithmetic inside is over a length already validated
# against it.
#
# easily-swappable-parameters - the per-target kernels take (pointer, count,
# wanted), two of which are integers. No caller writes that signature: it is
# reached only through the std::span overloads, where the count comes from the
# span and cannot be transposed with the size being asked for.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
    -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
    -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
